  "content": "And\n\n[Verse 1]\n[Dm]who are you, the\nproud lord said, that\nI must bow so\n[C]low?\n[F]Only a cat of a\n[F]different coat, that's\n[Gm]all the truth I\n[Am]know. In a\n\n[Verse 2]\n[Dm]coat of gold or a\ncoat of red, a\nlion still has\n[C]claws, And\n[F]mine are long and\nsharp, my lord, as\n[Gm]long and [Am]sharp as\n[Dm]yours.\nAnd\n\n[Chorus]\n[Dm]so he spoke, and\n[Am]so he spoke, that\n[Dm]lord of Casta-\n[Am]mere, But\n[Bb]now the rains weep\n[Gm]o'er his hall, with\n[Bb]no one there to\n[Dm]hear. Yes\n[Bb]now the rains weep\n[Gm]o'er his hall, and\n[Bb]not a soul to\n[Dm]hear.\n\n[Solo Cello]\n[Dm]\n[C]\n[F]\n[Gm]\n[Dm]\nAnd\n\n[Chorus]\n[Dm]so he spoke, and\n[Am]so he spoke, that\n[Dm]lord of Casta-\n[Am]mere, But\n[Bb]now the rains weep\n[Gm]o'er his hall, with\n[Bb]no one there to\n[Dm]hear. Yes\n[Bb]now the rains weep\n[Gm]o'er his hall, and\n[Bb]not a soul to\n[Dm]hear.",
